# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# Dependencies. No leading slash: `infra/pulumi` will carry its own node_modules alongside the
# root one. A root-anchored pattern would leave that untracked but not ignored, which is one
# `git add -A` away from committing it.
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*

# Testing
coverage/
/output/

/data

# Build output
build/
/bin
dist/
.tsbuild/

# ...but `scripts/build/` holds the tooling that *produces* build output, not the output itself.
# Without this negation the pattern above swallows it silently: `git add` reports nothing, the
# file never lands, and the first clean clone discovers it when the script it needed is missing.
# The same trap exists in .prettierignore and eslint.config.mjs; all three are negated together.
!scripts/build/

# Pulumi. State lives in the local file backend (`pulumi login --local`), and stack config may
# carry encrypted secrets — but Pulumi.<stack>.yaml itself is committed.
.pulumi/

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.pnpm-store/
.eslintcache

# Env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example
